<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 26 March, from 1484 to 1995.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/william-caxton" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-caxton.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1484">1484 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">542 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Caxton prints his English translation of Aesop's Fables</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s first printer completed his edition of the 'Fables of Esope' at Westminster, illustrated with woodcuts. Caxton's books helped standardise written English.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1812">1812 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">214 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake devastates Caracas and Venezuela</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Holy Thursday a powerful earthquake destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracas">Caracas</a> and other towns held by the young republic, killing thousands. Royalist clergy called it divine punishment, and the First Republic soon fell.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1827">1827 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">199 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ludwig van Beethoven dies in Vienna</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Beethoven died aged 56 during a thunderstorm. Despite growing deafness he composed nine symphonies and late string quartets that changed Western music, and some 20,000 people attended his funeral.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bangladesh declares independence from Pakistan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Pakistani army's crackdown in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a>, independence was proclaimed in the name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sheikh-mujibur-rahman">Sheikh Mujibur Rahman</a>. Nine months of war followed, and Bangladesh won its freedom in December 1971.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Egypt and Israel sign a peace treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the White House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> and Menachem Begin signed the first peace treaty between Israel and an Arab state, building on the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords. Israel returned the Sinai by 1982.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1995">1995 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">31 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Schengen Agreement abolishes border checks in Europe</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Seven European countries, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, removed passport controls at their common borders. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schengen-area">Schengen Area</a> now covers most of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> and several other states.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
